From: Sebberich <sebberich@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:11:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/27] Mobile: Add Bluetooth nearby sync for shopping lists
 (Android)

Native module that advertises a rotating per-list token, scans, and runs
a GATT server and client (coded PHY when available). The protocol in
TypeScript authenticates members via the list key, exchanges item
summaries and pushes the same signed events as the relay sync; the
status circle turns yellow while searching and green with found/total.
Wire protocol documented in lists/nearby/PROTOCOL.md.

